      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a risky approach; promising the impact of a direct manufacturing tax credit as a \"massive industry win\" could make the Senator feel deceived if he later discovers the cost projections suggest job losses or instability. You should instead frame Section 4b as an aggressive target-specific mechanism that directs every dollar toward high-volume domestic production to immediately unlock the subsidy flows your clients rely on. A more effective talking point would acknowledge the short-term friction but pivot quickly to how this specific design accelerates long-term stability and attracts the private capital Vance cares about most.",
